                    insight_rebalanced:     `Portfolio rebalanced: you hit the €2.57M contribution target inside the 5,600-day ceiling, ranked by contribution per faculty-day, focused on one credible new franchise, and defended the 28% anchor with a real quid pro quo. Revenue, relevance and impact moved together — and the plan survived the Q4 shock because you built in resilience.`,
                    insight_overcapacity:   `Capacity blown: you booked faculty past 100% to make the number on paper. When the senior instructors cut days, cohorts get cancelled mid-delivery and refunds follow — the contribution you booked never lands. The 5,600-day ceiling is the one constraint the board told you was fixed.`,
                    insight_anchorlost:     `Anchor lost: stripping the academy to fund the new bet turned a renewing 28% client into a €1M+ hole. No growth sector closes that gap in a single year — the concentration risk you were warned about crystallised on your watch.`,
                    insight_concede:        `Margin surrendered: conceding the anchor's 12% with no quid pro quo erased ~€320k of contribution — two-thirds of your entire gap — in one signature. Retention is a negotiation, not a surrender; you trained the client to squeeze you again.`,
                    insight_scatter:        `Spread too thin: funding all four growth sectors overran the faculty ceiling and left every launch below critical mass. Focus is a capacity decision, not a preference — one credible franchise beats four nobody remembers.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed result: some moves landed, but the mix, pricing, growth bet and anchor defence didn't fully reinforce each other — enough slippage that the +25% target stayed just out of reach or the portfolio's resilience is in doubt.`,
                    insight_revenue:        `You ranked by revenue, not yield: protecting the biggest line instead of the highest contribution per faculty-day meant scarce capacity kept feeding the academy all game. The wrong metric in Q1 quietly capped what every later quarter could deliver.`,
                    insight_funnel:         `You cut the discovery funnel: axing both under-filled flagships on standalone margin removed the channel 40% of your academy clients first came through. The pipeline thins next year even though this year's spreadsheet looked cleaner.`,
                    insight_gap:            `The +25% target stayed out of reach: the moves were defensible but didn't compound to €0.50M of new contribution within the ceiling. Closing it needed the yield tilt, the right pricing tier, and a focused growth bet all pulling together.`,
                    insight_tight:          `You hit the target running faculty right at the ceiling: efficient, but with almost no slack. That is the efficiency-versus-resilience tension — a little headroom is what lets you absorb the next shock without cancelling cohorts.`,
